# Maintain scalable searchable Music DNA revisions

- Design for a very large Music DNA library: versioned profiles, source provenance, deduplication, bulk ingestion, resumable jobs, fast text and facet search.
- Respect existing SQLite schema and FTS/inverted indexes in src/music-dna.mjs; benchmark before replacing a proven storage engine.
- Use canonical source and recording checksums when available to dedupe, but preserve distinct live/studio/remaster versions.
- Record observed vs inferred status and current revision; keep earlier profiles/revisions available.
- Batch with bounded concurrency and idempotent upsert/transaction behavior; never re-download or reprocess unchanged assets unnecessarily.
- Support indexed genre/mood/instrument/vocal text filters plus BPM/year/duration filtering when data is grounded.
- Do not claim massive bulk analyses have been run unless actual jobs, profile counts and error metrics confirm it.
